Fix: "KV Transfer metrics: ..." log line unreadable at typical
VLLM_LOG_STATS_INTERVAL, e.g.:

    KV Transfer metrics: vllm:kv_offload_cpu_cache_usage_perc=0.0,
    vllm:kv_offload_cpu_cache_write_usage_perc=0.0, ...
    vllm:kv_offload_lookup_sync_delay_seconds_sum=0.013403591030510142, ...

(distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/metrics.py,
KVConnectorLogging.log() -- shared by every KV connector type, not just
the offloading one this deployment uses).

Root cause: `xfer_metrics_str = ", ".join(f"{k}={v}" for k, v in
xfer_metrics.items())` dumps every key at full float repr precision
(Python's default float-to-str, 17 significant digits worst case) and
every key regardless of whether it's zero this interval -- an idle
cache's *_usage_perc=0.0 triplet, empty histograms, etc. Every connector
type's metric keys share a "vllm:" Prometheus-style prefix, repeated on
every single key for no informational value in a log line (as opposed to
a Prometheus scrape, where the prefix matters).

Fix: strip the "vllm:" prefix, format floats to 4 significant figures
(str.format's %.4g) instead of full repr, and skip zero-valued entries
(both int 0 and float 0.0) -- a metric that's genuinely idle this
interval isn't worth a line entry; if nothing non-zero was observed, skip
the log line entirely instead of printing an empty "KV Transfer metrics:
". Purely a formatting change: `reduce()`'s underlying dict and every
connector's stats collection are untouched, so Prometheus metrics
(scraped separately, not from this string) are unaffected.

Also (follow-up in the same session, requested separately): the line had
no on/off switch at all -- VLLM_LOG_STATS_INTERVAL only controls *how
often* it fires, not whether it fires. Added `_METRICS_LOG_ENABLED =
os.environ.get("VLLM_KV_TRANSFER_METRICS_LOG", "1") != "0"`, matching
VLLM_KV_TRANSFER_LOG / v1/kv_offload/transfer_log.py's existing
convention (read once at import, on by default). The accumulator is
still reset every interval regardless of the gate, so disabling the log
line doesn't leave stats accumulating unbounded -- only the `log_fn(...)`
call itself is skipped.
--- a/distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/metrics.py
+++ b/distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/metrics.py
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 # SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project
+import os
 from dataclasses import dataclass, field
 from typing import Any, TypeAlias, TypeVar
 
@@ -14,6 +15,15 @@
 
 logger = init_logger(__name__)
 
+# request-logging: gate for the periodic "KV Transfer metrics: ..." INFO
+# line (KVConnectorLogging.log(), below) -- independent of
+# VLLM_LOG_STATS_INTERVAL, which only controls how *often* it fires, not
+# whether it fires at all. Matches VLLM_KV_TRANSFER_LOG / v1/kv_offload/
+# transfer_log.py's convention: read once at import, on by default. The
+# Prometheus metrics themselves (KVConnectorProm, elsewhere in this file)
+# are untouched by this switch -- it only silences the log line.
+_METRICS_LOG_ENABLED = os.environ.get("VLLM_KV_TRANSFER_METRICS_LOG", "1") != "0"
+
 
 @dataclass
 class KVConnectorStats:
@@ -99,10 +109,29 @@
             # Produce a single cumulative stats object for the last time
             # interval from the recorded observations.
             xfer_metrics = self.transfer_stats_accumulator.reduce()
-            xfer_metrics_str = ", ".join(f"{k}={v}" for k, v in xfer_metrics.items())
-            log_fn("KV Transfer metrics: %s", xfer_metrics_str)
-
-            # Reset metrics for next interval
+            # request-logging readability fix: the raw dict has full-precision
+            # float reprs (e.g. "0.013403591030510142") and every zero-valued
+            # metric (most intervals have several, e.g. an idle cache's
+            # *_usage_perc=0.0), making the line unreadable at typical
+            # interval counts. Drop the shared "vllm:" prefix (every key
+            # across every connector type has it -- pure noise here), round
+            # floats to 4 significant figures, and skip zero-valued entries
+            # (a metric that fired is still shown at 0 via its sibling
+            # _count; a metric that's simply idle this interval isn't worth
+            # a line entry).
+            if _METRICS_LOG_ENABLED:
+                xfer_metrics_str = ", ".join(
+                    f"{k.removeprefix('vllm:')}="
+                    f"{f'{v:.4g}' if isinstance(v, float) else v}"
+                    for k, v in xfer_metrics.items()
+                    if v
+                )
+                if xfer_metrics_str:
+                    log_fn("KV Transfer metrics: %s", xfer_metrics_str)
+
+            # Reset metrics for next interval (independent of the log gate
+            # above -- the accumulator must not grow unbounded just because
+            # the line is silenced).
             self.reset()
 
 
